==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
By this point in the game, you should have the [[Aqua Crystal]] and all Superior [[Treasure]] in [[Empire of Cats]] as I.M. Phace's fast attack rate and high damage can pose a significant threat. Try not to attack the enemy base too early, as I.M. Phace is tough and can kill you quickly if you are not prepared.

I.M. Phace has long range, longer than that [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]], but still not enough to hit [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]], so use them as your main attackers. In addition, [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]] is resistant to I.M. Phace and has the weaken ability, so bring it as well if you have it. I.M. Phace outranges [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Neo Psychocat]], but he still comes in handy preventing the Imperator Saels from destroying your meatshields too quickly.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
The main threat in this stage is not actually Galactic Overseer Nyandam, but rather the Cyberhorns, which have over 400,000 health and 10,000 DPS even with all the [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] accessable at this point. However, due to their extremely low range and speed, you can stall them easily by Slowing/Freezing them.

2-3 meatshields, [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Neo Psychocat]] and/or [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]], [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Wheel Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]]/[[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] and any fast unit such as [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Swimmer Cat]].

All cats should be around level 20.

[[Battle Items]]: Sniper the Cat, Rich Cat (Optional)

Send out a few Wall Cats to stall the Croco, Kroxo and Jackie Pengs. Once Mistress Celeboodle comes out, kill her with appropriate meatshielding and a Paris or Dragon. Mistress Celeboodle should drop enough money to send out Bahamut and Wheel Cat with some Psychocats.

At this point, the first Cyberhorn should have spawned. Once he reaches somewhere around the middle, spam cats with the following priority: Meatshields > Debuffers > Attackers. Don't be too worried if the Cyberhorns kill your meatshields too fast, as long as there are a steady stream of debuffers, the Cyberhorn won't advance too far. Your wallet will be filled along the way with Mistress Celeboodles. As you slowly kill the Cyberhorn, Nyandam may advance and kill some of your meatshields. This is fine as long as you keep spamming them.

You should have killed the first Cyberhorn when the second one comes out, take the time for it to advance to the frontline and spam attackers to chip Nyandam. Nyandam will proceed to kill everything, and then you can start your stack again and kill the second Cyberhorn. Rise and repeat until Nyandam dies. Then just destroy the enemy base.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
At this point, you should have plenty of [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien units]]. Obviously, collecting as many Anti-Alien treasures as possible (500%) is pretty much required and should be priority to weaken Bun Bun. While Bun Bun Symbiote may seem intimidating at first, he can easily be defeated with cats like [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]] and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sadako Cat]].

Bun Bun Symbiote has low range, although the [[Wave Attack]] he creates is often long enough to reach most, if not all of your backliners. It should be made obvious that all variants of Bun Bun have high attack power, so too many waves will end the battle quickly. If you have Sadako Cat's [[True Form]], it can be used to prevent the wave, however, the wave occurs very rarely, so it won't bring a lot of benefit unless your luck is against you. However, it still outranges Bun Bun and can weaken him, providing an advantage. Using medium-long range cats like [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] will prove effective. However, be aware that [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Wheel Cat]] does ''not'' outrange Bun Bun, not even in his True Form, so avoid wasting money and slots on him. Use any [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] that you have, because most of them will likely outrange Bun Bun.

(Note: You should have at least 400% Anti-unstarred treasures before attempting this strategy)

3 75¢ meatshields, Castaway Cat, Macho Legs Cat, Cameraman Cat, Paris Cat, fill the rest of the slots with cats that may help.

Send out the meatshields to stall the incoming peons, stack Castaway Cats while slowly upgrading your wallet to max, after stacking about 5 Castaways, start spamming everything until Bun Bun Symbiote is dead, if your cats are not too low-leveled, you should win automatically.

